  "summary_en": "European Parliament JURI study by Bertolini on AI and civil liability. It argues regulation must be technology-specific, rejects electronic personhood, critiques the Product Liability Directive and the Expert Group report, and proposes a Risk-Management Approach imposing strict liability on the best risk controller, applied to industrial robots, connected driving, medical robots and drones.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AI regulation should be technology-specific, not unitary, given AI's heterogeneity.",
   "Proposes a Risk-Management Approach: strict liability on the party best able to control the risk.",
   "Electronic personhood is rejected or assessed only functionally, class-by-class.",
   "The Product Liability Directive needs reform on software, defect, development risk and damages.",
   "Applies the approach to industrial robots, connected and automated driving, medical robots and drones."
  ],
